The 07:03 scheduled fire never actually produced a new run. list_task_runs showed
only one run ever logged against catalyst-method-weekly-blogs, still marked
"running" since 11 September, because last week's scheduled session stayed open
as an ordinary chat afterwards (the image-crop fix, mostly). The scheduler saw an
existing run in progress and skipped firing a fresh one this week. Confirmed by
trying run_scheduled_task by hand, which the harness itself refused with "This
tool is unavailable in unattended sessions". So this week's batch was written and
published inside that same long-lived session instead, on request.

If a scheduled-task session is going to be kept open for follow-up chat, expect
next Friday to skip too unless that session gets closed out first. Move ordinary
follow-up conversation to a new chat rather than continuing in a scheduled run's
session, or the routine stalls silently with no error surfaced anywhere obvious.

Also removed all visible publish dates from the site this run, on Harry's
instruction (commit a521ca9, just before this batch): blog cards, the article
page header, and datePublished from the BlogPosting schema. publishedAt stays in
lib/manual-posts.ts since sorting and the SeoBot date-override logic still need
it. See CLAUDE.md for the note.

